IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cccfa-types`
IMPORT `cccfa-dates`

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — GOAL 1: CANCELLATION AND
-- DISCLOSURE PERIODS.
--
--   "Was the debtor's cancellation made in time, and how long may a
--    continuing disclosure period run?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_52.txt — ss 18, 27, 29.

§ `Goal 1 — cancellation and disclosure periods`

-- s 27 "(1) A debtor ... may cancel the contract by giving written notice ...
-- within 5 working days of the day that disclosure is made under section 17
-- (or at any time if that disclosure has not been made) and either,— (a) in
-- the case of a contract referred to in subsection (2), paying the cash price
-- ... within 15 working days of the day the notice is given; or (b) in any
-- other case, returning ... any advance and any other property ... within 5
-- working days of the day that disclosure is made under section 17 (or at any
-- time if that disclosure has not been made)." "Within n working days of" a
-- day: by the nth working day after it (fork F1).
@ref s 27(1)
GIVEN c IS A Cancellation
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to cancel` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `initial disclosure made on`
    WHEN JUST disclosed THEN JUST (`the` 5 `th working day after` disclosed `, Matariki days` (c's `cancellation Matariki days`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 29 "(1) Section 27 does not apply if the credit is provided for a
-- specified period of less than 2 months and no part of the credit is used,
-- with the knowledge of the creditor, to pay amounts owing to the creditor or
-- a related company under another credit contract. ... (3) Section 27 does not
-- apply to a layby sale agreement."
@ref ss 27, 29
@export Whether a debtor's cancellation of a consumer credit contract is effective under ss 27-29 of the Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (NZ): written notice within 5 working days of initial disclosure (at any time if none was made), and either the cash price paid within 15 working days of the notice (for the credit sales in s 27(2)) or the advance and property returned within those 5 working days; never for credit under 2 months that does not refinance the creditor, or for a layby. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A Cancellation  @desc The disclosure date, the notice date, the kind of contract, when the cash price was paid or the advance returned, the s 29 facts and Matariki days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cancellation is effective` c IF
        NOT c's `credit for less than 2 months, not refinancing the creditor`
    AND NOT c's `a layby sale agreement`
    AND within (c's `notice of cancellation given on`)
    AND (IF   c's `a credit sale of a kind in s 27(2)`
         THEN CONSIDER c's `cash price paid on`
              WHEN JUST paid THEN paid AT MOST `the` 15 `th working day after` (c's `notice of cancellation given on`) `, Matariki days` (c's `cancellation Matariki days`)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER c's `advance and property returned on`
              WHEN JUST returned THEN within returned
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    WHERE
        GIVEN x IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        within x MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day to cancel` c
            WHEN JUST last THEN x AT MOST last
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 18 "(2) The maximum period for a continuing disclosure statement is,—
-- (a) in the case of a revolving credit contract, 45 working days; or (b) in
-- any other case, 6 months." A period of 45 working days beginning on day S
-- ends on the 45th working day counted from S; 6 months beginning on S end
-- under the Legislation Act 2019 s 56 (fork F2; the month-end case changed
-- after the independent pass).
@ref s 18(2); Legislation Act 2019 s 56
GIVEN start IS A DATE, revolving IS A BOOLEAN
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest end of a continuing disclosure period beginning on` start `, revolving` revolving `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    IF   revolving
    THEN `the` 45 `th working day after` (`the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` start) `, Matariki days` matariki
    ELSE `the last day of a period of` 6 `months beginning with` start
